<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Stayscape</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h3>edit your listing</h3>
    <form method="POST" action ="/listings/<%=listing._id %>?_method=PUT">
    <input name="listing[title]" value="<%= listing.title %>"type="text"/>
    <textarea name="listing[description]"> <%= listing.description %></textarea>
       <br><br>
       <input type="number" name="listing[price]"value="<%= listing.price %>" type="number">
       <br><br>
       <input type="text" name="listing[image]" value="<%= listing.image %>" type="text">
       <br><br>
       <input type="text" name="listing[location]"value="<%= listing.location %>" type="text">
       <br><br>
       <input type="text" name="listing[country]"value="<%= listing.country %>" type="text">
       <br><br>
       <button>Update Listing</button>
    </form>
</body>
</html>


<%# action-Where should I send the form data after the user clicks Submit?%>
<%# The browser knows that whatever the user types in this input belongs to the key country because of the name="country" 
attribute. When the form is submitted, Express receives it as req.body.country.%>
<%# The value attribute shows the current (existing) value inside the input box. value takes priority over placeholder. %>